---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Serafim | Privacy Policy"
  description="How the Serafim social app handles your personal data."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <h1 class="h2">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: October 25, 2026.</p>

      <p class="body-copy">
        This Privacy Policy explains how the developer of Serafim ("the
        Developer", "we", "us", "our") collects, uses, stores, shares and protects
        your personal information when you use the Serafim Service. It should be
        read together with the Terms of Service, which govern your use of the
        app. We apply the data protection principles of Malawi's Data Protection
        Act and similar laws, and GDPR-style principles where they apply to users
        in the European Union or European Economic Area.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We collect the following personal information when you use Serafim:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Account information: your Serafim user ID, the email address you
          signed up with, and - when you sign in with Google - your Google
          account identifiers and the profile details Google shares with us.
        </li>
        <li>
          Profile information: your display name, username, bio, profile photo,
          interests, friend and follower relationships, and the privacy settings
          you choose, such as who may send you friend requests or add you to
          groups.
        </li>
        <li>
          Content you create: posts, comments, chat messages and media
          attachments, reactions (sparks), and group information.
        </li>
        <li>
          Device and technical information: device identifiers, operating system
          and version, app version, IP address, push notification tokens, and
          diagnostics.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We do not knowingly collect precise GPS location or payment information.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use your information</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We use your information to create and authenticate your account, store and
        deliver content and messages, operate feeds, circles, groups and chats,
        send notifications, enforce our rules and keep the Service safe, and
        understand how the Service is used so we can improve it.
      </p>

      <h2>Legal bases for our use</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We process personal data on the basis of consent (for example when you
        sign up and accept the Terms), the performance of a contract with you, our
        legitimate interests in operating and securing the Service, and legal
        obligations. We apply data protection principles - lawfulness and
        legitimacy of processing, purpose limitation, data minimisation, accuracy,
        storage limitation, integrity and confidentiality.
      </p>

      <h2>How we share information</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We do not sell your personal information. We share it only with the service
        providers that help us run the Service - including authentication, hosting,
        storage, cloud and push notification providers - and with other users when
        you share content with them, such as a post visible to your circles or a
        message delivered to a friend. We may also disclose information where
        required by law or to protect the rights and safety of people.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We keep your account information and content for as long as your account
        is active and needed to provide the Service. You can delete individual
        messages or posts from within the app; chat messages also have a per-device
        retention setting (by default they are kept). Chat backups you save to
        Google Drive are handled by Google. When you delete your account, we delete
        or deactivate the associated personal data, subject to any retention
        obligations under applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We use reasonable technical and organisational measures - including
        encryption in transit and access controls - to protect your information.
        No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot
        guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete,
        export or object to the processing of your personal data, and to withdraw
        consent. These rights may be provided directly by the data protection law
        that applies to you - including the GDPR for users in the European Union
        or European Economic Area, and Malawi's Data Protection Act. To exercise
        them, contact the Developer through the Serafim GitHub repository. You
        also have the right to lodge a complaint with the relevant data protection
        authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Serafim is not directed at children below the minimum age described in the
        Terms of Service. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
        children. If we learn that we have collected it, we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Your information may be processed in Malawi and by service providers that
        may be located outside Malawi, including in other countries. Where data
        crosses borders, we rely on appropriate safeguards.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We may update this Privacy Policy. The current version is always available
        in the app and is marked with a date. Your continued use of the Service
        after a change takes effect means you accept the updated Policy. Questions
        about this Policy can be sent to the Developer through the Serafim GitHub
        repository.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Contact the Developer through the
        <a class="prose-link" href={site.repo}>Serafim GitHub repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    display: grid;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  /* Quiet section heads: the h1 carries the page scale. */
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }
  .legal-meta {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
</style>
